{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487377-should-paradox-continue-their-partnership-with-cog-choice-of-games","id":1487377,"title":"Should Paradox continue their partnership with COG (Choice of Games)?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-21T06:37:56-07:00","id":1487377,"title":"Should Paradox continue their partnership with COG (Choice of Games)?","content":"The three VTM COG games that deal kind of exclusively with VTM are Night Road, Parliament of Knives, and Sins of the Sire. Theres Out for Blood, but thats more of a Hunters game.<br /> <br /> Night Road was a great game, and although it has little replayability, it's still pretty fun the first few times, my favourite build being the social gangrel. I haven't bought Parliament of Knives yet, but it has very positive steam reviews, and the demo was super fun. Now sins of the sire is the worst out of all three if we go by steam, and after playing the demo, I had to kind of agree, the steam revies go more depth into this if you want to check that out. But hopefully they learned from their mistakes.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen, besides Sins of the Sire, Parodoxes parthnership with COG (Choice of Games) has given us some pretty great stuff. And I know that other games such as Bloodhunt has done pretty well, but this partenrship in itself feels pretty profitable as well. I also feel this is a good way to build up the VTM, and overall the WOD, fanbase.<br /> <br /> In your opinion, do you think they should continue the partnership? Or better yet, do you think they -will- continue that partnership?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-21-2022, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T12:13:40-07:00","id":1487408,"title":"","content":"Yes. I'd rather play a video game, but unless they use 2000s technology, I can't anyway, so this is a good single player means to interact with the WoD. I have no idea what they'll do with it in the future. I think <i>Night Road</i> has unfairly overshadowed the other stories, which could spell diminishing returns for future products, but <i>Sins of the Sire</i> is clearly unfinished. So maybe new products could depict the brand favourably, if Paradox is worried about that. They don't seem be rushing the <i>Parliament of Knives </i>DLC, which has been leaked, but still not published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T04:21:53-07:00","id":1487719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487377-should-paradox-continue-their-partnership-with-cog-choice-of-games?p=1487408#post1487408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I'd rather play a video game, but unless they use 2000s technology, I can't anyway, so this is a good single player means to interact with the WoD. I have no idea what they'll do with it in the future. I think <i>Night Road</i> has unfairly overshadowed the other stories, which could spell diminishing returns for future products, but <i>Sins of the Sire</i> is clearly unfinished. So maybe new products could depict the brand favourably, if Paradox is worried about that. They don't seem be rushing the <i>Parliament of Knives </i>DLC, which has been leaked, but still not published.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the dlc ever get greenlit? Only thing I found about it was the writer trying to get the idea approved back in December. Was pitched to add 2 clans and 2 new romances as the 4 big additions but haven't seen anything about it since.<br /> <br /> Update: There was a claim of a beta leak on mobile that reveal the two new clans as Lasombra and Malkavian. Possibility of a late summer release according to users on the steam forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","user":"Syren1987","date":". 07-24-2022, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26090-syren1987","name":"Syren1987","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}